I replaced the linear scan with a one-time direct lookup table indexed by message number, preserving the first matching entry for duplicates. This makes every `GetMesg` call O(1) after the first initialization.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const MESG* table[65536] = {0};
    static bool initialized = false;

    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; ++i)
        {
            const FIT_UINT16 n = mesgs[i].num;
            if (table[n] == NULL)
                table[n] = &mesgs[i];
        }
        initialized = true;
    }

    return table[num];
}
```